{"absent":["No function bodies, exports or entry points appear in these fragments.","No struct or union layouts appear in these fragments.","No locking rules or concurrency contracts appear in these fragments.","No state machine transitions beyond start and busy polling are described.","No timing, sequencing or error recovery procedures are described.","No interrupt handling or DMA behavior is described."],"dossier":"D17","findings":[{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_ID"],"text":"Chipcommon JTAG master control provides a master enable and a separate external target enable, while serial flash control is anchored at a fixed low register offset. The master enable is one, the external enable is two, and the flash control offset is hex 40."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_OPCODE","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_ACTION","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_CS_ACTIVE","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_START","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_BUSY"],"text":"Flash control packs an opcode selector in the low byte, an action selector in the next three bits, a chip select active flag valid on newer revisions, and a shared top bit that starts an operation and reads back as busy. Masks are low byte for opcode, bits nine through eleven for action, bit twelve for chip select active, and the top bit for start or busy."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_START","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_BUSY"],"text":"Software starts a serial flash operation by setting the top control bit and polls that same bit until it clears, because start and busy are the same hardware bit rather than separate fields."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_ST_WREN","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_ST_WRDIS","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_ST_RDSR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_ST_WRSR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_ST_READ","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_ST_PP","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_ST_SE","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_ST_BE","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_ST_DP","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_ST_RES","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_ST_CSA","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_ST_SSE"],"text":"ST flash operations use fixed encodings where write enable is hex 6 and disable is hex 4, status read is hex 105 and status write is hex 101, data read is hex 303 and page program is hex 302, sector erase is hex 2D8 with subsector variant hex 220 and bulk erase hex C7, deep power down is hex B9, signature read is hex 3AB, and keep chip select asserted is hex 1000."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_READ","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_PAGE_READ","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_STATUS","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_BUF1_WRITE","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_BUF2_WRITE","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_BUF1_ERASE_PROGRAM","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_BUF2_ERASE_PROGRAM","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_BUF1_PROGRAM","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_BUF2_PROGRAM","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_PAGE_ERASE","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_BLOCK_ERASE","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_BUF1_WRITE_ERASE_PROGRAM","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_BUF2_WRITE_ERASE_PROGRAM","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_BUF1_LOAD","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_BUF2_LOAD","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_BUF1_COMPARE","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_BUF2_COMPARE","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_BUF1_REPROGRAM","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHCTL_AT_BUF2_REPROGRAM"],"text":"Atmel style flash uses its own fixed operation encodings with paired buffer one and buffer two variants for write, erase program, program, write erase program, load, compare and reprogram, plus distinct codes for continuous read, page read, status query, page erase and block erase. Documented values run from hex 7E8 for read and 7D2 for page read through status 1D7, buffer writes 384 and 387, erase programs 283 and 286, programs 288 and 289, page erase 281 and block erase 250, write erase programs 382 and 385, loads 253 and 255, compares 260 and 261, and reprograms 258 and 259."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHADDR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHDATA"],"text":"Serial flash address and data windows follow the control register at the next two word offsets, namely hex 44 for address and hex 48 for data."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHDATA_ST_WIP","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHDATA_ST_WEL","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHDATA_ST_BP_MASK","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHDATA_ST_BP_SHIFT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHDATA_ST_SRWD"],"text":"ST status observed through flash data reports write in progress in bit zero, write enable latch in bit one, a three bit block protect field starting at bit two, and a status register write disable in the top bit. Masks are hex 1, hex 2, hex 1C with shift two, and hex 80."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHDATA_AT_READY","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHDATA_AT_MISMATCH","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHDATA_AT_ID_MASK","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASHDATA_AT_ID_SHIFT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_BCAST_ADDR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_BCAST_DATA"],"text":"Atmel status observed through flash data reports ready in the top bit, compare mismatch in bit six, and a small device identifier field masked by hex 38 and shifted by three. Chipcommon also provides broadcast address and data registers at hex 50 and hex 54 for fanning one write to many targets."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOPULLUP","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOPULLDOWN","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOIN","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOOUT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOOUTEN","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOCTL","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOPOL","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOIRQ","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_WATCHDOG"],"text":"General purpose pins expose separate registers for pullup and pulldown selection on newer revisions, input sampling, output driving, output enabling, pin mux control, polarity selection and interrupt status, followed by a watchdog register. Pull controls sit at hex 58 and 5C, pin registers step from hex 60 through hex 74, and watchdog is at hex 80."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOTIMER","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOTIMER_OFFTIME","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOTIMER_OFFTIME_SHIFT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOTIMER_ONTIME","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOTIMER_ONTIME_SHIFT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOTOUTM","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CLOCK_N","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CLOCK_SB","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CLOCK_PCI","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CLOCK_M2","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CLOCK_MIPS"],"text":"A low power LED timer on newer cores splits one word into low half off time and high half on time with shifts zero and sixteen, plus an output mask register. Timer is at hex 88 with off mask hex FFFF and on mask hex FFFF0000, mask register at hex 8C, and five clock controls for N SB PCI M2 and MIPS at hex 90 94 98 9C and A0."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CLKDIV","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CLKDIV_SFLASH","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CLKDIV_SFLASH_SHIFT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CLKDIV_OTP","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CLKDIV_OTP_SHIFT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CLKDIV_JTAG","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CLKDIV_JTAG_SHIFT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CLKDIV_UART","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CAP_EXT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CAP_EXT_SECI_PRESENT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CAP_EXT_GSIO_PRESENT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CAP_EXT_GCI_PRESENT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CAP_EXT_SECI_PUART_PRESENT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CAP_EXT_AOB_PRESENT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_PLLONDELAY","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FREFSELDELAY"],"text":"Clock divider control at hex A4 dedicates separate subfields to serial flash, OTP, JTAG and UART dividers with documented masks and shifts, while an extension capability register at hex AC reports presence of SECI, GSIO, GCI, SECI UART and always on block features. Divider masks are hex F000000 shift 24 for serial flash, hex F0000 shift 16 for OTP, hex F00 shift 8 for JTAG and hex FF for UART. Presence bits are one, two, four, eight and hex 40 respectively, with PLL on and reference delays at hex B0 and B4."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SLOWCLKCTL","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SLOWCLKCTL_SRC","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SLOWCLKCTL_SRC_LPO","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SLOWCLKCTL_SRC_XTAL","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SLOECLKCTL_SRC_PCI","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SLOWCLKCTL_LPOFREQ","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SLOWCLKCTL_LPOPD","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SLOWCLKCTL_FSLOW","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SLOWCLKCTL_IPLL","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SLOWCLKCTL_ENXTAL","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SLOWCLKCTL_XTALPU","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SLOWCLKCTL_CLKDIV","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SLOWCLKCTL_CLKDIV_SHIFT"],"text":"Slow clock control at hex B8 on mid revisions selects among LPO, crystal and PCI sources, configures LPO frequency and power, forces slow operation, controls PLL ignore and crystal management, exposes crystal running status, and carries a high half clock divider. Source encodings are zero for LPO, one for crystal and two for PCI, with frequency, power down, force slow, ignore PLL, enable crystal and crystal up bits at hex 200, 400, 800, 1000, 2000 and 4000, plus divider mask FFFF0000 shift 16."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SYSCLKCTL","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SYSCLKCTL_IDLPEN","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SYSCLKCTL_ALPEN","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SYSCLKCTL_PLLEN","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SYSCLKCTL_FORCEALP","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SYSCLKCTL_FORCEHT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SYSCLKCTL_CLKDIV","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SYSCLKCTL_CLKDIV_SHIFT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CLKSTSTR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_EROM"],"text":"System clock control at hex C0 manages idle and active low power enables, forced PLL on, forced ALP and forced HT requests, plus a high half divider for the low power clock. Enable and force bits are one, two, four, eight and hex 10, with divider mask FFFF0000 shift 16. Clock status observation is at hex C4 and the EROM pointer at hex FC."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_PCMCIA_CFG","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_PCMCIA_MEMWAIT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_PCMCIA_ATTRWAIT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_PCMCIA_IOWAIT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_IDE_CFG","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_IDE_MEMWAIT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_IDE_ATTRWAIT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_IDE_IOWAIT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_PROG_CFG","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_PROG_WAITCNT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASH_CFG","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASH_CFG_DS","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_FLASH_WAITCNT"],"text":"Parallel attachment timing uses groups of config plus memory attribute and IO wait registers for PCMCIA starting at hex 100, IDE starting at hex 110, and a programmable interface at hex 120, with parallel flash config at hex 128 and its wait count at hex 12C. Parallel flash data width is selected by bit hex 10 where clear means eight bit and set means sixteen bit."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL_START","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL_BUSY","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL_OPCODE","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL_OP_READ","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL_OP_WRITE","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL_OP_WRDIS","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL_OP_WREN","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL_OTPSEL","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL_OTP_PRESENT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL_LOCK","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL_SIZE_MASK","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL_SIZE_1K","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL_SIZE_4K","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL_SIZE_16K","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL_SIZE_SHIFT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SROM_CONTROL_PRESENT"],"text":"Serial ROM control at hex 190 reuses the top bit as both start and busy, dedicates two bits to operation selection among read, write, write disable and write enable, and reports OTP selection, OTP presence, lock, size and device presence in low bits. Operation codes are zero, hex 20000000, 40000000 and 60000000 with opcode mask 60000000, while size uses mask 6 shift 1 with zero for one K, two for four K and four for sixteen K, plus bits hex 10, 20, 8 and 1 for OTP select, OTP present, lock and present."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOPULLUP","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOPULLDOWN","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_GPIOTIMER","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_CLKDIV","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SLOWCLKCTL","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_SYSCLKCTL","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_HW_WORKAROUND","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_PMU_STRAPOPT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_PMU_XTAL_FREQ"],"text":"Several registers are valid only on restricted core revisions, so drivers must gate access by revision instead of probing unconditionally. Pull controls and hardware workaround need revision twenty or later, LED timer needs sixteen or later, strap needs twenty eight or later, divider and system clock need three or later with slow clock limited to six through nine, and crystal frequency needs PMU revision ten or later."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_4706_FLASHSCFG","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_4706_FLASHSCFG_MASK","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_4706_FLASHSCFG_SF1","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_4706_FLASHSCFG_PF1","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_4706_FLASHSCFG_SF1_TYPE","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_4706_FLASHSCFG_NF1","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_4706_FLASHSCFG_1ST_MADDR_SEG_MASK","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_4706_FLASHSCFG_1ST_MADDR_SEG_4MB","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_4706_FLASHSCFG_1ST_MADDR_SEG_8MB","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_4706_FLASHSCFG_1ST_MADDR_SEG_16MB","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_4706_FLASHSCFG_1ST_MADDR_SEG_32MB","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_4706_FLASHSCFG_1ST_MADDR_SEG_64MB","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_4706_FLASHSCFG_1ST_MADDR_SEG_128MB","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_4706_FLASHSCFG_1ST_MADDR_SEG_256MB"],"text":"A 4706 specific flash structure register at hex 18C reports second flash presence and first flash address window size. Low bits flag second serial, second parallel, second serial type with zero for ST and one for Atmel, and second NAND, while the high nibble of the low byte encodes first window size from four through two hundred fifty six megabytes. Masks are hex FF overall and F0 for size, presence bits one two four and eight, sizes hex 10 20 30 40 50 60 70."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_NFLASH_CTL","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_NFLASH_CTL_ERR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_NFLASH_CONF","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_NFLASH_COL_ADDR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_NFLASH_ROW_ADDR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_NFLASH_DATA","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_NFLASH_WAITCNT0"],"text":"A compact legacy NAND interface occupies words starting at hex 1A0 for control with an error flag at bit hex 8000000, configuration, column and row addresses, data, and first wait count."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_HW_WORKAROUND","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_UART0_DATA","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_UART0_IMR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_UART0_FCR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_UART0_LCR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_UART0_MCR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_UART0_LSR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_UART0_MSR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_UART0_SCRATCH","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_UART1_DATA","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_UART1_IMR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_UART1_FCR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_UART1_LCR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_UART1_MCR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_UART1_LSR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_UART1_MSR","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_UART1_SCRATCH"],"text":"A hardware workaround register sits at hex 1E4, followed by two identical UART blocks each with data, interrupt mask, FIFO control, line control, modem control, line status, modem status and scratch registers. First UART spans hex 300 through 31C and second spans hex 400 through 41C in four byte steps."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_PMU_CTL","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_PMU_CTL_ILP_DIV","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_PMU_CTL_ILP_DIV_SHIFT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_PMU_CTL_RES","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_PMU_CTL_RES_SHIFT","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_PMU_CTL_RES_RELOAD","include/linux/bcma/bcma_driver_chipcommon.h::BCMA_CC_PMU_CTL